  "body": "Allocated memory reported from jemalloc appears to be significantly under-reported in our install, preventing cache autotuning from working at all.  The actual process memory usage and tracked cache memory usage appear correct but the jemalloc stats, although growing roughly the same, appear totally out of sync; jemalloc allocated memory:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"2201\" alt=\"Screenshot 2022-08-19 at 16 06 40\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1026154/185650741-7ed2f11e-6304-406b-8bbe-a04519445872.png\">\r\n\r\nAnd per-cache(+total) memory reported by synapse:\r\n<img width=\"2128\" alt=\"Screenshot 2022-08-19 at 16 06 33\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1026154/185650815-998108b4-2d49-48a8-9780-0787bbe1f3fc.png\">\r\n\r\nActual process memory:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1230\" alt=\"Screenshot 2022-08-19 at 16 10 50\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1026154/185650844-67ba1a34-ba94-421e-84f1-f2af436ae21f.png\">\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nUnsure if this is an environment or code related issue or perhaps something in jemalloc (seems unlikely).",
